.TH RFID 1
.SH NAME
rfid \- read, write, copy and emulate 125 kHz RFID tags
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBrfid\fR [\fB\-r\fR] [\fB\-n\fR \fItries\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIfile\fR] [\fB\-c\fR \fB125\fR|\fBpsk\fR|\fB134\fR]
\fBrfid write\fR [\fB\-n\fR \fIn\fR] [\fB\-pass\fR \fIhex\fR] [\fB\-with\fR \fIhex\fR] [\fB\-lock\fR] [\fB\-em4305\fR] \fIprotocol\fR \fIhex\fR ...
\fBrfid write\fR [\fIoptions\fR] \fB\-f\fR \fIfile\fR
\fBrfid copy\fR [\fB\-n\fR \fIn\fR] [\fB\-pass\fR \fIhex\fR] [\fB\-with\fR \fIhex\fR] [\fB\-lock\fR]
\fBrfid emulate\fR \fIprotocol\fR \fIhex\fR ...
\fBrfid emulate \-f\fR \fIfile\fR
\fBrfid clear\fR [\fB\-with\fR \fIhex\fR] [\fB\-n\fR \fIn\fR]
\fBrfid dump\fR [\fB\-with\fR \fIhex\fR] [\fIblock\fR]
\fBrfid list\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Rfid
works with the 125 kHz tags (cards, key fobs) held to the back of the
Flipper, through
.BR /dev/rfid .
It knows the 25 protocols of the Unleashed firmware (liblfrfid,
.BR "rfid list" ):
EM4100 (RF/64, /32, /16), Electra, H10301, Idteck, Indala26, IoProxXSF,
AWID, FDX-A, FDX-B, HIDProx, HIDExt, Pyramid, Viking, Jablotron, Paradox,
PAC/Stanley, Keri, Gallagher, Nexwatch, Radio Key, GProxII, Noralsy and
Indala224.
A tag's data is given and shown as the stock app does: the protocol's
bytes in hex (the \fBData:\fR line of a \fB.rfid\fR file).
.PP
Without a command
.B rfid
reads a tag and prints its protocol and bytes, then the data as the
stock app's info screen shows it (facility code, card number...):
.PP
.nf
.ft B
	$ rfid
	EM4100 04 00 98 3D C5
	  FC: 152 Card: 15813 CL:64
	  DEZ 8: 09977285
	  DEZ 10: 0009977285
.ft R
.fi
.PP
EM4100 at RF/64 is read by its own decoder first, as before; every
other tag goes through all the protocols' decoders, and a protocol counts
only when it gave the same bytes several times in a row (as stock).
Today only the protocols that modulate the field's amplitude (ASK:
Manchester, biphase, direct; the READ column of
.BR "rfid list" )
can be read: FSK and PSK ones need a longer capture and another carrier
from the kernel (planned).
Exit status 0 when a tag was read.
.TP
.B \-r
also print the edge timings of each read (µs).
.TP
.BI \-n " tries"
reads of half a second (default 4; up to three times as many while a
protocol has been seen but not yet confirmed).
.TP
.BI \-o " file"
also save the tag as a \fB.rfid\fR file (the stock format;
\fBKey type:\fR is the protocol's name).
.SS "write, copy"
.B "rfid write"
makes a blank tag (a T5577, the common kind; else an EM4305, as stock)
carry the given tag: the protocol's own block layout (Unleashed's
write_data), the data blocks first and the configuration last.
.I Protocol
is a name of
.B "rfid list"
(case, spaces, \- and / do not matter:
.BR em4100_32 ,
.BR "radiokey" ;
.B EM
is EM4100);
.I hex
its bytes, one per word (\fB00 DE AD\fR) or run together
(\fB00DEAD\fR), or
.B \-f
a \fB.rfid\fR file.
A tag of an ASK protocol is read back and the write repeated until it
reads right (\fB\-n\fR rounds, default 20); FSK and PSK tags are
written once and reported as not read back.
.B "rfid copy"
reads a tag, waits for it to go, and writes it to the blank one put on
next.
.TP
.BI \-pass " hex"
give the T5577 that password too: nothing rewrites it without it.
Write it down.
Not for protocols that fill block 7 (HIDExt, Indala224).
.TP
.BI \-with " hex"
the password the tag has now.
.TP
.B \-lock
set the T5577 lock bit: the blocks can never be written again.
.TP
.B \-em4305
write an EM4305 only (the protocols that have an EM4305 layout).
.SS emulate
.B "rfid emulate"
makes the Flipper be that tag for a reader, until Ctrl-C.
The reader's field is the clock: the kernel loads the antenna in step
with its carrier (RFIDIOCEMU), so nothing drifts and the CPU is idle.
One frame must fit 512 segments today: the ASK protocols do (EM4100,
Electra, FDX-B, Viking, Jablotron, PAC/Stanley, Gallagher, Radio Key,
GProxII, Noralsy); FSK and PSK frames are 540 to 3534 (planned).
.SS clear, dump
.B "rfid clear"
removes a T5577 password (no password, \fB\-with\fR, then a list of the
passwords cloners set);
.B "rfid dump"
reads one T5577 block.
.SS list
The protocols with their maker, modulation, bit rate, data size and
whether they can be read today, and the heap the decoders take during a
read.
.SH FILES
.TP 20
.B /dev/rfid
the antenna (group gui)
.TP
.B /home/lfrfid
where the RFID app keeps its \fB.rfid\fR files
.SH NOTES
The protocol code is the Unleashed firmware's (lib/lfrfid, GPLv3),
compiled unchanged.
